241 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 242 0 R/Alt(Three shaded views of the seed 0 CAD model. Left: the test article alone, a rectangular box of square aluminum tubes about 616 by 382 by 272 mm with two long rails and three cross members in each of the top and bottom frames joined by four corner posts; three dark steel blocks stand for the lumped masses, and four short tubes carry small blocks at their ends, the components with their tip masses, marked with orange triangles; open black squares mark the four mount points at the bottom corners. Middle: the article bolted at its four mounts to a larger flat grid frame of tan tubes carrying five lumped masses; nine orange stars on the host frame mark where the service forces act and two pink crosses on the article mark the two weaker forces applied to it directly. Right: the article on four thin suspension cords at its mounts, with six blue cylindrical shaker bodies, each with a stinger and a black arrow showing its force direction; blue filled circles mark the control gauge points, open orange diamonds the held-out gauge points and orange triangles the component tips.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[43]/Pg 895 0 R>>
endobj
