406 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 407 0 R/Alt(Two panels. Left: the force spectra of the six shakers of the 6-shaker, 12-control test with the line law, from 20 Hz to 2 kHz, in decibels relative to the largest; each shaker has its own color and line style and is labeled with its node and axis (25 Z, 8 Z, 22 Z, 39 X, 52 Y, 47 Y). The drives rise and fall by 30 to 40 dB across the band, with sharp peaks and notches near the article's modes. Right: the single-axis vertical specification for seed 0, in decibels relative to its peak. Gray thin lines are the four mount spectra line by line; blue open circles, squares, diamonds and downward triangles are their one-third-octave band values; a green dotted line is the mean of the four mounts; a thick orange solid line is the straight-line envelope, which touches the highest band at several frequencies and lies well above the mean elsewhere.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 900 0 R>>
endobj
