<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 422 0 R/Alt(Two scatter plots side by side, random on the left and shock on the right. Each point is one simulated test run with an inverse control law. The horizontal axis is the control error in decibels on a log scale; the vertical axis is the mean element stress error in decibels, positive meaning over-test. Orange filled squares, rigs with as many shakers as controls, sit at control errors from about 0.01 to 1 dB and stress errors of about +4 to +23 dB in random and +3 to +15 dB in shock. Green open triangles, the rig with more shakers than controls, sit at near-zero control error and stress errors within a few decibels of zero. Blue open circles, rigs with fewer shakers than controls, sit at control errors of about 2 to 9 dB and stress errors of about -8 to +3 dB.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 901 0 R>>
endobj
