<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 456 0 R/Alt(Three panels of dot plots, one row per metric, for the random study. The horizontal axis is the Spearman rank correlation with element stress error, from -0.3 to 1. Blue filled circles are control gauges and orange open triangles are held-out gauges, joined by a gray line. In the left panel, all multi-shaker cases, held-out gauges lead every metric, by about 0.25 to 0.35. In the middle panel, rigs with unequal shaker and control counts, the two markers nearly coincide for every metric; the summed autospectra in one-third-octave bands is highest at about 0.8. In the right panel, the line law on all rigs, every control metric sits near -0.1 while held-out metrics reach 0.48 to 0.84. The Annex C global error is lowest in every panel.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[13]/Pg 902 0 R>>
endobj
