<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 506 0 R/Alt(Two panels, random on the left and shock on the right. Each of five rows is a base input on the same rigid base: envelope of the four mounts, mean of the four mounts, the true mount-averaged motion one axis at a time, the true motion three axes at once, and all twelve mount translations as in service. A blue filled circle marks the mean element stress error and an orange open downward triangle the 5th percentile, joined by a gray line, with thin ticks for each seed. In random the means are +9.41, +2.94, -3.64, -2.08 and about 0 dB; in shock +5.38, +1.85, -6.57, -5.32 and about 0 dB. Only the envelope keeps the 5th percentile above zero.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 904 0 R>>
