536 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 537 0 R/Alt(Three panels. Panel a: for each of seven rigs with unequal shaker and control counts, gray open circles show the paired difference in element stress error, band law fitted in decibels minus line law, for each of twenty seeds, and a blue diamond the mean: 3 x 6 -0.05, 3 x 12 -1.23, 3 x 24 -1.80, 6 x 12 +0.12, 6 x 24 -0.34, 12 x 6 -0.29, 12 x 24 +0.32 dB; negative means the band law is better. Panels b and c: the worst control one-third-octave band over-test, mean over cases, for four models (true model converged; frequencies +1 percent, first shot; frequencies +3 percent, first shot; damping halved, first shot). The line law is an orange solid line with filled circles, the band law fitted in power a green dotted line with open squares, the band law fitted in decibels a blue dashed line with open triangles. With unequal counts the line law runs 17 to 23 dB, the decibel-fitted band law 11 to 16 dB, the power-fitted band law 5 to 12 dB. With equal counts the line law rises from 2 dB converged to 22 and 31 dB on a first shot, while both band laws stay at or below about 11 dB.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[12]/Pg 905 0 R>>
endobj
