581 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 582 0 R/Alt(A square scatter plot. Each point is one test on a rig with unequal shaker and control counts, twenty seeds. The horizontal axis is the level raise that leaves 5 percent of elements under-tested, which needs the stress truth; the vertical axis is the level raise set by rule P from the held-out gauges. Orange open circles are the line law, mean 5.4 against 5.3 dB; blue open triangles are the band law fitted in decibels, mean 4.3 against 5.1 dB. A solid diagonal marks rule equals truth and dotted lines mark 2 dB either side. The points scatter widely about the diagonal, many of them more than 2 dB away.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[11]/Pg 907 0 R>>
endobj
